Optimal Solution - Compute the maximum product subarray by scanning from both directions and resetting products on zeros.
                  Negative numbers can flip signs, so scanning from both left and right ensures we don’t miss the maximum product.

class Solution {
    public int maxProduct(int[] nums) {
        int n = nums.length;
        // Product from left to right
        int leftProd = 1;
        // Product from right to left
        int rightProd = 1;
        // Initialize answer with first element
        int ans = nums[0];
        // Traverse from both ends
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            // Reset product if it becomes zero
            leftProd = (leftProd == 0) ? 1 : leftProd;
            rightProd = (rightProd == 0) ? 1 : rightProd;
            // Multiply current elements
            leftProd *= nums[i];
            rightProd *= nums[n - 1 - i];
            // Update maximum product found so far
            ans = Math.max(ans, Math.max(leftProd, rightProd));
        }
        return ans;
    }
}

Time Complexity :- O(n).
Space Complexity :- O(1).
